  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical cavity is made in a lead sphere of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> such that its surface touches the outside surface of lead sphere and passes through the centre. The shift in the centre of mass of the lead sphere as a result of this hollowing, is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/27826.JPG\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 149px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
